: 10, "prompt": "What does the phrase ‘for that same reason’ refer to?\n(A) the anxiety that patients feel during therapy\ncomplaints from patients who feel unsupported\n(c) the conflicting ethical concerns of neuroscientists\n(0) Psychotherapists who take on unsuitable patients\nScanned by CamScanner", "sourcePage": 79, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 549}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "In the fourth paragraph, we learn that the drug called DCS\n(a) is unsafe to use except in small quantities.\nhelps to control only certain types of phobias.\n(c) affects how neurons in the brain react to stimuli.\n(D) increases the emotional impact of certain events.", "sourcePage": 80, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "The writer suggests that propranolol may\n(a) not offer a permanent solution for patients’ phobias.\nincrease patients’ tolerance of key triggers.\nbe inappropriate for certain phobias.\n(c) produce some beneficial side-effects.\n©\nScanned by CamScanner", "sourcePage": 80, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 894}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "What does the word ‘it’ in the sixth paragraph refer to?\n(A) a placebo treatment\nthe disease process itself\n(c) a growing body of research\n(D) a genuine biological response", "sourcePage": 84, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 293}, {"number": 21, "prompt": "What does the writer tell us about Ader’s and Evers’ studies?\n(a) Both involve gradually reducing the dosage of a drug.\nEvers is exploiting a response which Ader discovered by chance.\n(c) Both examine the side effects caused by immunosuppressant drugs.\n() Evers is investigating whether the human immune system reacts to placebos as\nAder’s rats did.", "sourcePage": 84, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 473}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "According to Charlotte Blease, placebos are omitted from medical training because\n(a) there are so many practical subjects which need to be covered.\nthose who train doctors do not believe that they work.\n(c) they can be administered without specialist training.\n(D) their effect is more psychological than physical.", "sourcePage": 84, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 830}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-52b0f84a004bc59b437f", "filename": "practice book 2 .pdf", "sha256": "52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [92, 93, 95, 96, 97]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "52b0f84a004bc59b-p94", "label": "Part A · practice book 2 .pdf", "part": "A", "sourceSha256": "52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06", "pages": [94], "questions": [], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-52b0f84a004bc59b437f", "filename": "practice book 2 .pdf", "sha256": "52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/52b0f84a004bc59b437fc5180b9ea2c35097362c5b9b9ea4d9a282d5cbbecf06.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [95, 96, 97]}], "passages": []}]}
